Ozone draws its notification widgets at the scale the display DPI suggests,
which on a 1280x960 four-inch panel is too small to read at arm's length.

This cannot move to menu_widget_scale_factor: that setting is applied inside
gfx_display_get_dpi_scale() for every menu driver at once, and the call site
below is now shared by every driver that is not XMB. The multiplier has to be
gated on the driver, and there is no per-driver widget scale setting upstream.

diff --git a/gfx/gfx_widgets.c b/gfx/gfx_widgets.c
--- a/gfx/gfx_widgets.c
+++ b/gfx/gfx_widgets.c
@@ -1224,7 +1224,10 @@ static void gfx_widgets_update_layout(
       scale_factor                  = gfx_display_get_dpi_scale(
             p_disp,
             settings, width, height, fullscreen, true);

+   if (p_disp->menu_driver_id == MENU_DRIVER_ID_OZONE)
+      scale_factor                  = scale_factor * 1.500f;
+
    /* Check whether screen dimensions, menu scale factor or the
     * notification font have changed. The font is watched here rather
     * than from a settings callback because the rebuild needs the
